Disco Code
==========

Disco Code is an open source, local-inference coding agent distributed under the
MIT License. It is a derivative work combining two upstream MIT-licensed
projects. This file records which parts of the tree derive from which upstream,
so that license inheritance is auditable.

Both upstreams are MIT licensed, and MIT permits derivative works and
relicensing under the same terms provided the original copyright and permission
notices are retained. Disco Code therefore remains MIT and reproduces both
notices in LICENSE.


Upstream 1: Claw Code
---------------------
Source:    https://github.com/ultraworkers/claw-code
Version:   v0.1.3
License:   MIT
Copyright: (c) 2026 UltraWorkers and Claw Code contributors

Derived components:

    crates/api/              LLM transport layer and provider abstraction
    crates/commands/         Slash-command surface
    crates/compat-harness/   Compatibility test harness
    crates/plugins/          Plugin discovery, hooks, lifecycle
    crates/runtime/          Session, permissions, policy engine, MCP,
                             sandbox, prompt construction, compaction
    crates/telemetry/        Local telemetry primitives
    crates/tools/            Built-in agent tool implementations
    crates/rusty-claude-cli/ Terminal client
    crates/claw-analog/      Config, doctor, agent surfaces
    crates/claw-rag-service/ Local retrieval/embedding service

The prompt-construction pipeline in crates/runtime/src/prompt.rs is inherited
from Claw Code and is central to Disco Code's answer quality. It is retained and
extended rather than replaced.


Upstream 2: opencode
--------------------
Source:    https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode
Version:   v1.18.10
License:   MIT
Copyright: (c) 2025 opencode

Derived components are introduced in later phases and will be recorded here as
they land, covering the user interface layer, session presentation, and
supporting developer experience. opencode is TypeScript/SolidJS; Disco Code
consumes its interface layer as the webview frontend of a Tauri shell while the
Rust crates above remain the core.


Deliberate exclusions
---------------------
Neither upstream's cloud-model integrations are inherited. Disco Code performs
inference exclusively against a local Ollama daemon. Hosted-model providers,
their credential/OAuth flows, and hosted billing or account infrastructure are
removed rather than disabled, and an egress policy prevents cloud AI endpoints
from being reached at runtime.

Specifically, the following Claw Code components are not carried forward:

    crates/api/src/providers/anthropic.rs   Anthropic Messages API client
    crates/mock-anthropic-service/          Mock Anthropic service used to
                                            exercise the above
    crates/api/tests/client_integration.rs  Anthropic wire-protocol test suite
    rusty-claude-cli mock parity harness    Parity tests against the mock

along with, inside retained files, the xAI/OpenAI/DashScope endpoint
configurations and their credential handling, the hosted model registry and its
aliases, the subscription-provider OAuth token flow, and the `/login`,
`/logout`, and `/api-key` command surfaces. Remote MCP server authentication is
unrelated to the above and is retained.

The Claw Code retrieval service previously embedded repository contents through
a hosted endpoint by default; it now embeds against the local daemon, so
indexing a repository does not transmit source code.

This is a local-inference product, not an offline one. Network access for web
search, web fetch, code search, and Model Context Protocol servers is expected
and supported.
